    "review": "On June 21, 1970 at Berkeley’s Pauley Ballroom, the Dead delivered a high‑octane rock set that still feels fresh today. From the opening “Frozen Logger” through the electrifying “Easy Wind,” the band rode a wave of energy, culminating in a rare Not Fade Away → Saint Stephen segue that fans still talk about. Garcia was in a laid‑back, creeper‑influenced mood, even pulling a moaning solo on “Candyman” that earned nods from listeners. The rhythm section kept things tight, with an odd gunshot‑like percussive burst cutting through the Saint Stephen jam, adding an unexpected flavor. While the audience recordings capture some haze and occasional dropouts typical of 1970 tapes, the performance’s vigor and standout moments outweigh the sonic imperfections.",
